completed_at: "2026-08-09T22:09:11.524Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 420
acceptance_criteria: Every command that accepts one positional item id also accepts --id as a compatibility alias; supplying both fails deterministically; the public SDK exposes one reusable item-address resolution primitive; contracts help completions and MCP parity declare the alias consistently; unknown-option recovery no longer points away from the selected command; tests cover get test files docs deps comments notes learnings and lifecycle commands without removing positional compatibility
goal: project management = context management
objective: Remove item-identifier grammar context from agent memory
value: One addressing convention works throughout an end-to-end PM loop
why_now: A current dogfood session burned repeated retries in create-note-test-close flows
parent: pm-mpbb
risk: medium
confidence: high
severity: medium
resolution: Introduced a shared item-addressing primitive and projected --id across all single-item commands.
expected_result: "Positional IDs and --id are equivalent, with deterministic conflicts when both are supplied."
actual_result: "Unit, integration, manual acceptance, contracts, completion, and replication gates verify the complete matrix."
