comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-09T20:27:22.194Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: searched all statuses for show/get/test --id rejection, positional recovery, flag consistency, and item addressing. The existing grammar and unknown-option items are broader or adjacent; none owns a shared identifier resolver across the single-item surface."
  "2026-08-09T21:43:38.147Z","harness:codex","Manual acceptance finding: the first temp-workspace pass proved get/comments/notes/learnings/files/docs/test --id and append ordering, then exposed close --id missing from the normalization set plus copy/focus misclassified as extension-only contract surfaces. Expanded the shared primitive to all single-item lifecycle commands and nested item complete/files discover paths; added copy/focus to the core runtime contract map; focused integration now passes."
  "2026-08-09T22:09:10.266Z","harness:codex","Evidence: one public SDK item-address resolver now projects --id across the complete single-item command matrix, detects positional conflicts, and feeds contracts/completions. Manual temp-workspace acceptance and broad integration coverage pass; copy/focus runtime contracts and bounded replication waivers are explicit."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-09T22:09:10.844Z","harness:codex","A grammar alias is a cross-surface contract change: normalization, errors, help, completion, runtime classification, and replication policy must move together."
